// pfodWeb NOTE: excludes GPIO17/21 (OLED SDA/reset) and GPIO45 (Vext
// power-gate) - see vendor pins_arduino.h. GPIO18 (also SCL_OLED) stays
// kept via the LED alias.
// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO0 tagged "button" - confirmed via Heltec
// Wireless_Paper_V0.4_Schematic_Diagram.pdf (switch S2, silkscreen
// "BTN-0", wired to net IO0/GPIO0; separate from the S1 hardware
// RESET/EN button which is not GPIO-readable).
// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO18 tagged "led_high" - confirmed via same schematic:
// LED1 (orange) + 330R series resistor wired from net "LED" (the GPIO18
// alias in pins_arduino.h) to GND, i.e. GPIO HIGH sources current and
// turns the LED on (active-high). LED_BUILTIN (GPIO35) was NOT tagged -
// no LED connection to GPIO35 appears anywhere in the schematic (that
// alias appears to be an unused vendor-template leftover), and GPIO35
// is already excluded from this board's chipGpios (existing
// pin-exclusion, left untouched). The other visible LED (LED2, orange)
// is the battery-charge indicator wired directly to the TP4054 charger
// IC's CHRG pin, not GPIO-controllable.
